literation of the C body rather than assuming propagation.)* |\"\n),\n(\n\"| E67 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | any `NaN` coordinate | all four `<` are false ⇒ `d0|d1|d2|d3 == 0` ⇒ `rc == 1` (**reports a collision**) |\",\n\"| E67 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | **every** coordinate `NaN` | all four `<` are false ⇒ `d0|d1|d2|d3 == 0` ⇒ `rc == 1` (**reports a collision**) |\\n| E67b | `c2AABBtoAABB` | a **single** `NaN` coordinate | only the comparisons that coordinate participates in become false. A pair separated on *both* axes still has a true `<` from the other axis ⇒ `rc == 0`; poisoning the *only* true comparison (e.g. `A.max.x` or `B.min.x` for a pair separated on x alone) flips `rc` to `1`. *(Verified against the C; the test derives the expected value from a transliteration of the C body.)* |\"\n),\n]\nfor a,b in subs:\n    assert a in t, a[:70]\n    t = t.replace(a,b,1)\n\nt = t.replace(\n\"Every non-excluded row (E1–E15, E20–E41, E43–E74 — **69 rows**) has a passing\",\n\"Every non-excluded row (E1–E15, E20–E41, E43–E74, plus the E60b/E65b/E65c/E67b\\nrefinements discovered while testing — **73 rows**) has a passing\")\np.write_text(t)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\ngrep -c '^| E' translation/ERRORS.md","description":"Correct E60/E65/E67 rows in ERRORS.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5065,"cache_read_input_tokens":238344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5065,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52e2a50b-da79-4c25-983e-9e31bbba2fc9","uuid":"b2944545-9d0c-4680-9daa-4cddefe2f274","timestamp":"2026-08-27T07:12:45.401Z"}
