{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7czhevkpebpva52s62whvb5grt2pzftkaqdtdqvdnfciytdtatiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases are complete. **84 tests pass, zero divergences between the C and Rust `.so`s.**\n\n## What I did\n\n**Phase A — mapped the surface** into three mechanically-derived artifacts in `translation/`:\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 38 `nm -D` symbols with C/Rust source line numbers\n- `ERRORS.md` — 83 rows from grepping every `return 0`, `switch` default arm, null check, unguarded division and `sqrtf` in the C\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 87 rows covering the option × input-shape cross-product\n\n**Phases B–D** — 84 differential tests in `translation/tests/`, all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` (never calling Rust directly), comparing `f32` by `to_bits()` and structs as raw bytes (all 152 bytes of `c2Simplex`, all 72 of `c2Proxy` including slots the C never writes). Symbol diff is empty in both directions.\n\n## Things worth flagging\n\n**No bug was found in the Rust.** It is bit-exact, including x86 SSE NaN-payload propagation — I confirmed the `mul_ss`/`add_ss`/`sub_ss`/`div_ss` helpers against GCC's actual instruction stream (destination operand per site) for 13 functions, then exhaustively swept 20⁴ = 160,000 special-value combinations through `c2Dot`/`c2Det2`.\n\n**Three findings were errors in my own reading of the C**, corrected in the artifacts rather than in the C:\n\n1. **`ERRORS.md` E17/E18 are UB, not defined behaviour.** I'd written them up as testable. A probe showed the C returning stack residue (`rc=+inf`, `outA=(-1.2e30, 3.09e-38)`) for 5 of 7 indices — `c2Proxy pA;` is uninitialised and `c2MakeProxy` only writes `verts[0..count)`. Moved to the excluded list with the evidence.\n2. **E60/E65/E67 over-generalised NaN propagation.** `c2Maxv` is `x > y ? x : y`, so a NaN in the *first* operand **loses and is discarded** — a NaN in `B.min` does not propagate through `c2Clampv`. Three tests initially failed on my predicted sentinel (never on C-vs-Rust). Rows split into E60/E60b, E65/E65b/E65c, E67/E67b, and those tests now derive the expected value from a transliteration of the C body.\n3. **E26 (`iter == 20`) is unreachable.** 3.4M randomized calls never exceeded `*iterations == 4`. The test now asserts both libraries' full iteration histograms and reachable maxima are identical.\n\n**Two harness issues I had to fix, both of which would have made \"all tests pass\" meaningless:**\n- `cargo test` does **not** emit the cdylib for `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`. On a clean tree the harness found no `.so`. It now builds it on demand into a side target dir (cargo holds a lock on `target/`).\n- I added `harness_selfcheck.rs`, which cross-compares C `c2Skew` against Rust `c2CCW90` and asserts the macro **panics** — plus `±qNaN` and `±0.0` — so the assertions are proven to fire.\n\nI also vendored `libloading` into `vendor/` so `cargo test` needs no network or warm registry cache, and verified all 6 configurations (3 feature invocations × release/debug) via `scripts/check_features.sh`. `c_src/` is untouched apart from the `build/` directory the task asked for. Volume on the last run: ~10⁸ paired calls."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":300154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":884,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52e2a50b-da79-4c25-983e-9e31bbba2fc9","uuid":"63c0745f-6a9a-44a4-9c9b-72c254597f96","timestamp":"2026-08-27T07:25:35.578Z"}
